When `dirs` is passed to find_library(), meson skips the plain `-l` probe
(the only search that goes through the cc-wrapper, and thus sees the -L
flags in NIX_LDFLAGS) and only searches the given directories plus the
compiler's built-in library paths. On native builds the external `lib_dir`
property is just its /usr/local/lib default, which never contains llhttp
(or http-parser) in Nix. Call find_library() without `dirs` on non-freebsd
systems, like tang v15 did, so wrapper-supplied library paths are honoured.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -92,7 +92,7 @@
 if host_machine.system() == 'freebsd'
   http_parser = compiler.find_library(http_lib, dirs : '/usr/local/lib')
 else
-  http_parser = compiler.find_library(http_lib, dirs: [lib_dir])
+  http_parser = compiler.find_library(http_lib)
 endif
 
 licenses = ['COPYING']
